&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps businesses extend their online presence into the physical world. Our mission is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as Stripe has made it to accept payments online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Terminal provides an integrated in-person payments platform spanning software, payment processing, device fleet management, and hardware. Our hardware portfolio includes Stripe-designed readers and accessories as well as devices from third-party hardware partners. Together, these products enable businesses to build reliable, differentiated in-person payment experiences across a broad range of use cases, countries, and operating environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced Product Manager to build the strategy, development, and expansion of Terminal’s hardware portfolio. This role will work across both first-party and third-party hardware, helping define the multi-year roadmap for the devices, accessories, and partner ecosystem that power Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with hardware engineering, firmware and software engineering, design, operations, logistics, partnerships, sales, finance, legal, and regional teams. This is a highly cross-functional role for someone who can connect customer needs, technical constraints, business strategy, and execution across user experience, device capabilities, cost, quality, reliability, supply, and time to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute a multi-year strategy and roadmap for Terminal hardware across Stripe-built devices, third-party devices, accessories, and emerging form factors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a clear point of view on where Stripe should build, partner, or expand its hardware portfolio to address customer needs, competitive gaps, and global market opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define product requirements, user journeys, and acceptance criteria for end-to-end hardware products from concept through validation, launch, and post-launch iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hardware, firmware, software, and quality engineering teams to guide development and deliver high-quality device experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with external OEM, ODM, and technology partners to evaluate product capabilities, define joint roadmaps, resolve technical issues, and deliver hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the continued global expansion of Terminal’s third-party hardware portfolio, including device availability, local payment-method support, certifications, distribution, pricing, and launch readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and lead the evaluation process for additional third-party hardware providers and build business cases for new device categories, accessories, connectivity, and specialized use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with Terminal users, sales teams, and partners to understand in-person payments workflows, product gaps, and opportunities to improve the device experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish success metrics for hardware products and partnerships, using customer feedback, adoption, device reliability, support signals, and financial performance to inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate product strategy, priorities, risks, and trade-offs clearly to cross-functional partners and Stripe leadership, traveling occasionally to partner sites or Stripe offices, including APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience or equivalent experience leading complex technology products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success shipping physical hardware, connected devices, embedded products, payments devices, consumer electronics, or similarly complex products from concept through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and driving product strategy, roadmaps, requirements, prioritization, and launch plans for technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with hardware, firmware, and software engineering teams and the ability to participate credibly in technical product and architecture discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in navigating trade-offs across customer experience, technical feasibility, reliability, quality, cost, supply, and launch timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hardware product-development and manufacturing processes, including prototype development, validation, production readiness, and sustaining lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external vendors, manufacturers, OEMs, ODMs, or other strategic technology partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-focused and analytical approach to product development, with experience leading cross-functional programs, creating alignment, and using evidence to set priorities and measure outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, commerce platforms, point-of-sale systems, or in-person payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a portfolio that includes both first-party products and third-party partner products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with sourcing, supply-chain risk, device pricing, unit economics, and global distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payment-device certifications, local payment methods, accessibility requirements, connectivity, or regulated hardware environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching products internationally or a technical background in electrical engineering, computer science, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our mission at Duolingo is to develop the best education in the world and make it universally available. It’s a big mission, and that’s where you come in!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Duolingo, you’ll join a team that cares about finding &lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.duolingo.com/tag/engineering/?utm_source=greenhouse.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=engblog_gh_091224&quot;&gt;innovative solutions to complex technical problems&lt;/a&gt;, running countless experiments (300+ at a time!) with our massive user base to make data-driven decisions, and educating our users and employees alike. You’ll have limitless learning opportunities, mentorship and collaboration with world-class minds, and a variety of projects with large scopes — while doing work that’s both fun and meaningful.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our life-changing mission to develop education for our half a billion (and growing!) learners around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;This is a high-impact, high-visibility Staff TPM role at the center of one of Duolingo&#39;s most strategic engineering initiatives: dramatically reducing the effort required to get results and doubling developer productivity across the organization. You&#39;ll lead this initiative in close partnership with the Developer Amplification (DevAmp) Area, a team dedicated to accelerating how engineers work through better tooling, streamlined processes, and modern engineering practices. AI is one important lever — but the goal is the outcome: step-change improvements in how fast and effectively Duolingo engineers can build. This role is for a builder and a change agent: someone who can define what &quot;doubling productivity&quot; means in practice, align leadership and engineering teams around it, and drive the transformation to completion. If you thrive in ambiguity, have a bias for outcomes, and can bring people along through significant organizational change, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧠&amp;nbsp; You will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the roadmap for doubling developer productivity across Duolingo — aligning engineering, product, and data science around a shared vision, sequencing the work, and holding teams accountable to measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Lead organizational change management as engineering teams adopt new ways of working — building alignment, communicating progress to executives and ICs alike, and helping teams internalize new processes and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Developer Amplification (DevAmp) Area leads to accelerate developer productivity through AI-powered tooling, ensuring programs have clear goals, measurable impact, and sustained momentum across engineering squads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the delivery of strategic, high-impact cross-functional initiatives from conceptualization to launch, operating with significant autonomy across multiple workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, product, data science, QA, and executive leadership to ensure communication and alignment; serve as the connective tissue between Duolingo strategy and day-to-day execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage deep technical expertise to develop detailed plans with key milestones and goals, identify and mitigate risks, resolve dependencies, remove blockers, and ensure timely and smooth launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and evangelize engineering practices that drive step-change improvements in developer productivity — coaching engineering leads and TPMs on new ways of working and how to measure their impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive decisions when difficult tradeoffs must be made, including those with cross-organizational or company-level impact; model how to navigate hard problems with analytical rigor and a calm, decisive presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify systemic issues impacting delivery efficiency company-wide and take swift, collaborative action to resolve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide and develop other TPMs and engineering leads, scaling best practices across teams and continuously improving how the organization operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✅&amp;nbsp; You have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a TPM, Engineering Lead, or Engineering Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. or M.S. in Computer Science or equivalent degree or experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading large-scale technical transformation programs with measurable organizational impact — you&#39;ve shifted how engineering organizations think and work, not just shipped projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and influence in a matrix environment — able to build conviction among skeptics, align competing priorities across senior leadership, and drive decisions without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical credibility — enough to challenge architectural assumptions, spot delivery risks early, and earn the trust of strong engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and implement detailed plans that account for ambiguity, dependencies, and technical complexity — and to re-plan quickly when things change, without losing team confidence or momentum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of standing up new programs or practices from scratch in ambiguous, high-visibility environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to relocate to Seattle, WA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⭐&amp;nbsp; Exceptional candidates will have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of software engineering, systems engineering, or similar hands-on technical experience, in addition to program management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong conceptual fluency in LLM-based products, AI infrastructure, and developer AI tooling - enough to ask the right questions, challenge technical assumptions, and identify delivery risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running programs that include machine learning, large datasets, or AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with AWS at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
